GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2017-05-09T12:59:05Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Use ManyToMany decorator alongside with PrimaryGeneratedColumn
Description: Let's say I have 3 classes / tables : 'Artist', 'Artwork' and 'Tag'. 
Artist and Artwork both have a ManyToMany relation with Tag. What I'd like to do is the following : 

```
class Tag {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    @ManyToMany(type => Artwork, artwork => artwork.tags)
    @ManyToMany(type => Artist, artist => artist.tags)
    id: number;
} 
```

```
class Artwork {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    id: number;
   
    @ManyToMany(type => Tag, tag => tag.id, {
        cascadeInsert: true
    })
    @JoinTable()
    public tags: Tag[];
  
}
```

```
class Artist {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    id: number;
   
    @ManyToMany(type => Tag, tag => tag.id, {
        cascadeInsert: true
    })
    @JoinTable()
    public tags: Tag[];
    
}
```

Currently, it doesn't seem to work: tags are created but relationship between Tag and Artwork / Artist is not saved in 'join' table . How could I manage to setup such a mechanism without having to implement 2 specific Tag classes (one for each class) ? 

By the way I'm using @next version of typeorm with mysql-driver.

Thank you and keep up the good work !


